      'Setup example: 12 card(s) per player.',
      "Rule example: In positive contracts (three, two, one, solo): declarer's side wins by taking at least 36 of 70 card points. In klop avoid taking points; in beggar-type contracts take no tricks; in valat take all tricks.",
      'Turn-flow example: 1. Deal: 6 to talon, 12 each in packets of 6 counter-clockwise. 2. Bidding: Forehand waits; others bid or pass; highest bidder is declarer. 3. Calling: In three/two/one declarer calls a king; holder is secret partner. 4. Talon exchange: Declarer takes 3, 2 or 1 card(s) per contract and discards same number. 5. Announcements: Bonuses (trula, kings, lowest-trump ultimo) or kontra. 6. Play: Forehand leads (or declarer in beggar+). Follow suit; if unable play trump. Highest trump wins. 7. Scoring: Contract plus difference and bonuses; cumulative; game ends by škis round or target.',
